    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n38455" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">prōcĭdentĭa</span></b> , ae,
			f.
		1. procido, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a falling down</i> or <i>forwards</i>
			of a part of the body out of its place, <i>a
			procidence</i>, <i>prolapse</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ani,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Cels.
					6, 6, 8 <i>fin.</i></span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">vulvarum,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Plin.
					23, 9, 81, § 161</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">sedis,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id.
					26, 8, 58, § 90</span></i>
			; cf. procido, P.
			a.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b>
			Gram. t. t. = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀντίπτωσις</span>, <i>the substitution of one case for another</i>,
					<i><span class="en">Prisc. 1099</span></i> P.</div>
